  Vulnerability: Modern MLOps and version control systems (such as DVC or MLflow) are specifically designed to snapshot and persist model weights, hyperparameters, and execution environments. If regulatory mandates require strict state-archiving for legal discovery, the exact internal state of a model at any given deployment can theoretically be retained and reproduced, neutralizing the problem of evidentiary evaporation.
